  "body": "Stacked on #993 (itself on #957); its diff shows their commits until they merge.\n\n## What changed\nA Face under an area turn is generated in the turned frame and turned back (`turn_path(.., -turn)`), but a refusal left `face_over` through `?` with its spot still in the turned frame. New `boundary_turn::face_over_back` runs `face_over` and carries a refusal's spot (and ghost, if any) back through the same `-turn` (`turn_refusal`, built on `GenError::map_location` / `map_ghost`; a ghost that cannot turn is dropped). Both call sites in `generate.rs` (the path and the air-entry re-run) use it. No turn: refusal untouched. Successful output is unchanged (`golden_cl` and `conformance` green).\n\n## Tests\nPinned by `operation::boundary_turn::law::a_refusal_from_the_turned_frame_names_its_spot_where_the_part_is`, `with_no_turn_the_spot_is_unchanged`, `a_ghost_turns_back_with_the_spot_and_a_plain_refusal_passes`. Quick gate `--base upstream/main`: 5 steps, 0 failed; clippy `-D warnings` clean on camcraft-app.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo end-to-end test through `generate`: today a spot refusal cannot arise under a turn (a turn comes only from an open chain, which drops the base's holes, and any surviving hole is forbidden, so `face_band_sane` refuses first without a spot). The unit test uses a real holed region through `face_over_back`. Details in `docs/decisions/1017-face-turn-refusal-spot.md`.\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: fix: a Face refusal under an area turn names its spot where the part is, not in the turned frame (#1017, PR #1023)\nFork synced at v0.17.0\n\nFixes #1017\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
